<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31320" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nūbēcŭla</span></b> ,
		ae, f.
		dim.
		nubes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little cloud</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 18,
				35, 82, § 356</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>something
			cloudy</i> or <i>dark, a dark spot</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala urina, in quā veluti furfures
					atque nubeculae apparent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 6, 19, § 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">smaragdi variā nubeculā
					improbati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					37, 5, 18, § 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nubeculae et caligationes suffusionesque
					oculorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					29, 6, 38, § 123</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">20, 7, 26,
				§ 61</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a gloomy expression
				of countenance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frontis tuae nubecula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 9, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
